  "schoolyard_use_notes": "This tree has thick, leathery leaves that are perfect for teaching about plant durability and water conservation. The leaves remain green year-round, making it a great example for lessons on evergreen species. Its bark peels in strips, providing material for discussions on tree growth and bark functions. The flowers are small and white, blooming in clusters that can be used to explain pollination.",
